  },
  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>z</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;denote the complex conjugate of a complex number&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math> and let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></msqrt></math>. In the set of complex numbers, the number of distinct roots of the equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>z</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mfenced><mrow><mover><mi>z</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is _______."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>z</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>So&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mover><mi>z</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></mfenced><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>z</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>z</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>z</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>z</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>z</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Also,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>z</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo><mover><mi>z</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>i</mi><mover><mi>z</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>y</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>x</mi></math></p><p>i.e.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></math></p><p>From&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></math>, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>or</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>i.e. the points are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}